# platformd-verifyd user-presence verification interface.
#
# Served on a system Varlink socket at $RUNTIME_DIRECTORY/io.platformd.Verify
# (/run/platformd-verifyd/io.platformd.Verify). No secret material crosses it.
interface io.platformd.Verify

# Challenge the calling user to prove presence now by running the platformd-verify
# PAM stack — fingerprint, face, security key or password, whatever the
# administrator configured. The user is the caller's own (taken from the peer
# credentials, never a claimed name), so a process may only verify itself. On
# success the verification is recorded with platformd-trustd, so the session's
# freshness reflects it. sessionId names the session to refresh (the caller's
# display session is used if it is empty or does not belong to the caller); with
# no resolvable session the call fails NoSession, since the verification would
# refresh nothing. reason is a short human-readable purpose. The PAM conversation
# runs in a worker and the reply arrives when the factor completes; one
# verification runs at a time — a concurrent request is refused Busy rather than
# queued against the same reader. verified is the outcome, method the PAM service
# that ran.
method VerifyUser(
        sessionId: string,
        reason: string
) -> (
        verified: bool,
        method: string,
        realtimeUSec: int
)

error PermissionDenied()
error VerificationUnsupported()
error NoSession()
error Busy()
